{"name":"Tardis Blue","hex":"#003b6f","fetched":"2026-10-13","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"tardis","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["Alternative form of Tardis."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/tardis"},{"term":"blue","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Adjective","definitions":["Of a blue hue.","Depressed, melancholic, sad."]},{"part":"Noun","definitions":["The colour of the clear sky or the deep sea; the colour midway between green and violet in the visible spectrum and one of the primary additive colours.","Anything coloured blue, especially to distinguish it from similar objects differing only in colour."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/blue"}],"entries":[{"title":"TARDIS","blocks":[{"text":"The TARDIS is a fictional hybrid of a time machine and spacecraft that has, since 1963, appeared in the British science fiction television series Doctor Who and its various spin-offs. While a TARDIS is capable of disguising itself, the exterior appearance of the Doctor's TARDIS typically mimics a police box, an obsolete type of telephone kiosk that was once commonly seen on streets in Britain in the 1940s and 50s. Its interior is shown as being much larger than its exterior, commonly described as being \"bigger on the inside\"."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/1/1a/Tardis_in_Snow.jpg/330px-Tardis_in_Snow.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/TARDIS"},{"title":"Blue","blocks":[{"text":"Blue is one of the three primary colours in the RGB (additive) colour model, as well as in the RYB colour model. It lies between violet and cyan on the spectrum of visible light. The term blue generally describes colours perceived by humans observing light with a dominant wavelength between approximately 450 and 495 nanometres. The clear daytime sky and the deep sea appear blue because of an optical effect known as Rayleigh scattering. An optical effect called the Tyndall effect explains blue eyes. Distant objects appear more blue because of another optical effect called aerial perspective."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/5/5a/Earth-in-true-color-himawari-09.jpg/330px-Earth-in-true-color-himawari-09.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Blue"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/c/cd/Ilford_Manor_Road_geograph-3065865-by-Ben-Brooksbank.jpg/500px-Ilford_Manor_Road_geograph-3065865-by-Ben-Brooksbank.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/c/cd/Ilford_Manor_Road_geograph-3065865-by-Ben-Brooksbank.jpg/1280px-Ilford_Manor_Road_geograph-3065865-by-Ben-Brooksbank.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/c/cd/Ilford_Manor_Road_geograph-3065865-by-Ben-Brooksbank.jpg/500px-Ilford_Manor_Road_geograph-3065865-by-Ben-Brooksbank.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AIlford_Manor_Road_geograph-3065865-by-Ben-Brooksbank.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/6/60/Here%27s_that_TARDIS_again%2C_SW5_-_geograph.org.uk_-_906215.jpg/500px-Here%27s_that_TARDIS_again%2C_SW5_-_geograph.org.uk_-_906215.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/6/60/Here%27s_that_TARDIS_again%2C_SW5_-_geograph.org.uk_-_906215.jpg/500px-Here%27s_that_TARDIS_again%2C_SW5_-_geograph.org.uk_-_906215.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AHere's_that_TARDIS_again%2C_SW5_-_geograph.org.uk_-_906215.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/